{% comment %}
  Renders the options for one filter group, supporting BOTH data sources:

  1. A native Search & Discovery filter (metafield / variant option / product
     attribute). Preferred when present - gives real counts.
  2. Otherwise, a comma-separated tag list. Uses the same `.vtag-filter`
     mechanism FABRIC/OCCASION already use on this page: the shared
     "APPLY FILTERS" button collects every checked tag and navigates to
     /collections/<handle>/tag-a+tag-b.

  So the merchant can set these up either way (or migrate from tags to
  metafields later) without any theme change.

  Params: native_filter, tag_list, current_tags, empty_note
{% endcomment %}
{% if native_filter != blank %}
  {% if group_colors %}
    {%- comment -%}
      The real Color filter lists every exact variant shade (BOTTLE-GREEN,
      OLIVE-GREEN, DARK-GOLD, COBALT-BLUE...) - 20+ raw checkboxes. Grouping
      them under simple families (Green, Blue...) via substring match on the
      label gives a shopper 8-ish broad choices instead. One family checkbox
      carries ALL its real shade values (data-color-values); vamas-collection.
      liquid's APPLY button expands that into one filter.v.option.color param
      per shade when building the URL. Anything that doesn't match a known
      family name still gets its own plain checkbox below, so no colour is
      ever unselectable.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign color_families = 'Black,Maroon,Gold,Green,Navy,Blue,Red,Pink,White,Grey,Purple,Yellow,Orange,Brown,Cream,Beige' | split: ',' -%}
    {%- assign param_name = native_filter.values.first.param_name -%}
    {%- assign assigned_values = '' -%}
    {% for family in color_families %}
      {%- assign family_down = family | downcase -%}
      {%- assign group_values = '' -%}
      {%- assign group_active = false -%}
      {% for value in native_filter.values %}
        {%- assign value_down = value.label | downcase -%}
        {%- if value_down contains family_down -%}
          {%- assign group_values = group_values | append: value.value | append: '||' -%}
          {%- assign assigned_values = assigned_values | append: value.value | append: '||' -%}
          {%- if value.active -%}{%- assign group_active = true -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {% endfor %}
      {% if group_values != '' %}
        <label class="filter-check-row">
          <input type="checkbox" class="vcolor-group-filter" data-color-param="{{ param_name }}" data-color-values="{{ group_values }}" {% if group_active %}checked{% endif %}>
          {{ family }}
        </label>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% for value in native_filter.values %}
      {%- assign probe = value.value | append: '||' -%}
      {% unless assigned_values contains probe %}
        <label class="filter-check-row">
          <input type="checkbox" name="{{ value.param_name }}" value="{{ value.value }}" {% if value.active %}checked{% endif %}>
          {{ value.label }} ({{ value.count }})
        </label>
      {% endunless %}
    {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
    {% for value in native_filter.values %}
      <label class="filter-check-row">
        <input type="checkbox" name="{{ value.param_name }}" value="{{ value.value }}" {% if value.active %}checked{% endif %}>
        {{ value.label }} ({{ value.count }})
      </label>
    {% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
{% elsif tag_list != blank %}
  {% assign group_tags = tag_list | split: ',' %}
  {% for t in group_tags %}
    {% assign tag_clean = t | strip %}
    {% if tag_clean != '' %}
      <label class="filter-check-row">
        <input type="checkbox" class="vtag-filter" value="{{ tag_clean | escape }}" {% if current_tags contains tag_clean %}checked{% endif %}>
        {{ tag_clean }}
      </label>
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
{% else %}
  <p class="filter-empty-note">{{ empty_note | default: 'Not set up yet.' }}</p>
{% endif %}
